face $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(2,3,1):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xyz-{z}^{2})\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xyz-{z}^{2})\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xyz-{z}^{2})\\text{ }k \\\\  & =yz\\text{ }i+xz\\text{ }j+(xy-2z)k \\\\ ∇\\,f(2,3,1) & =(3)(1)\\text{ }i+2(1)\\text{ }j+(2(3)-2(1))k \\\\  & =3\\,i+2\\,j+4k \\\\  & =⟨3,2,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(2,3,1)\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y-3,\\,z-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨3,2,4⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y-3,\\,z-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ 3(x-2)+2(y-3)+4(z-1) & =0 \\\\ 3x+2y+4z-16 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362470 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362471 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362470 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362472 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362470 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362473 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362470 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362474 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362470 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362475 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362470 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362470 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362470 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362471 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362470 1080 #uuid "ab905e04-ebcb-5bbc-8e7d-cdb57e6bb24a" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362471 1081 "3x+2y+4z-16=0" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362471 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362471 1084 #uuid "b9d90141-bb87-557b-8f42-7d4