[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\text{nullity}(A-4I)=2,$ there will be two eigenvectors that correspond to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =4,$ say, ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}.$ So, the generalized eigenvectors corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =4$ form the following chains: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\overset{A-4I\\,}{\\to }0 \\\\ {v}_{2}\\overset{A-4I\\,}{\\to }0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have *case II*, and $A$ has the following Jordan canonical form:\n\n$$\n{J}_{1}(4)\\,⊕\\,{J}_{1}(4)\\,⊕\\,{J}_{1}(1)=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n**Note:** The Jordan canonical form is unique up to the order of the Jordan blocks." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362757 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362758 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362757 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362759 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362757 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362760 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362757 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362761 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362757 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362762 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362757 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362757 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362757 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362758 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362757 1080 #uuid "f551173e-cdc5-55dd-9e6f-83961027a0a2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362758 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362758 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362758 1084 #uuid "b9aaaafa-9b58-5497-94c3-989324f52324" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362759 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362759 1083 #e