6362823 1081 "6.4" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362823 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362823 1084 #uuid "b3a04eeb-327b-5191-bf82-b02968049bf0" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362824 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362825 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362824 1069 "q-114684" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362824 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362824 1071 "Calculate $\\int (2x-{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x.$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362824 1072 #uuid "147de4a4-be73-51d2-8d4c-4cb4de81bc45" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362824 1074 "We can use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta \n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (2x-{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x & =\\int (2x-[{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x])\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (2x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2})-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362825 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362826 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362825 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362827 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362825 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362828 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362825 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362829 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362825 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362830 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362825 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362825 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362825 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362830 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362825 1080 #uuid "f2c0e43f-5343-57bc-ad26-cbe38057ac4f" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362826 1081 "{x}^{2}+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362826 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362826 1084 #uuid "53a1d31f-700b-57e3-bdcf-d8bd27643934" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362827 1081 "\\frac{1}{4}x-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362827 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362827 1084 #uuid "2b0d7a6c-1857-5d15-b705-b8fbaecb9afe" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362828 1081 "4x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362828 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362828 1084 #uuid "b63c4ee3-69f6-5431-b9f1-555a6275f486" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362829 1081 "\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362829 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362829 1084 #uuid "cf93c5be-e087-5294-b994-d0c21eda179c" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362830 1081 "{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362830 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362830 1084 #uuid "4e1376b1-e1ca-505c-b68c-6701296a0fe6" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362831 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362832 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362831 1069 "q-115947" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362831 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362831 1071 "Consider the section of the hyperbola $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=1$ that lies in the second quadrant. Given that $x=x(t),$ $y=y(t),$ and that $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=4$ on the hyperbola at the point where $x=-3,$ find the value of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}$ at that point." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362831 1072 #uuid "cc544fb2-b29c-5843-ace8-c118d11d787f" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362831 1074 "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3})-\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (\\frac{2x}{3})-\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot y & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=4$ and $x=-3.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\cdot (-2)-\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot y & =0 \\\\ -8-\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot y & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also want to substitute for $y,$ but we are not given this value. However, we can find it by substituting $x=-3$ into the equation of the hyperbola.\n\nAt the point where $x=-3,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(-3)^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & =1 \\\\ 3-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & =2 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4 \\\\ y & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we used $y>0$ since we're only interested in the second quadrant.\n\n Finally, substituting $y=2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-8-\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot 2 & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362832 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362833 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362832 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362834 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362832 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362835 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362832 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362836 13194139