ln}⁡(y)=2.$ Given that $x=x(t),$   $y=y(t),$  and that $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=2$ on the curve at the point where $x=\\frac{1}{2},$ find the value of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}$ at that point." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362838 1072 #uuid "04fc9383-ba9d-51b2-b7ff-6b5bffaa64a5" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362838 1074 "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{x}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y) & =2 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{x}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y)) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{x})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y)) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{x})+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y)) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{y}) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=2$ and $x=\\frac{1}{2}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2)\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}})+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{y}) & =0 \\\\ -8+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{y}) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also want to substitute for $y,$ but we are not given this value. However, we can find it by substituting $x=\\frac{1}{2}$ into the equation of the curve.\n\nAt the point where $x=\\frac{1}{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{x}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y) & =2 \\\\ 2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y) & =2 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(y) & =0 \\\\ y & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $y=1,$ we get  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-8+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (1) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362839 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362840 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362839 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362841 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362839 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362842 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362839 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362843 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362839 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362844 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362839 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362839 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362839 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362841 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362839 1080 #uuid "933d59db-68a6-5d20-bc41-310ebed025cc" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362840 1081 "\\frac{1}{8}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362840 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362840 1084 #uuid "ae467fb3-f63f-54bc-88d8-32c99fe9e08d" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362841 1081 "8" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362841 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362841 1084 #uuid "bd67acba-1d7d-5904-9fd2-988231e488fe" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362842 1081 "2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362842 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362842 1084 #uuid "b1b4a166-30db-52fa-98df-8a94aafd5f98" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362843 1081 "\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362843 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362843 1084 #uuid "3d267227-97a9-5d1c-9990-ea64e0fab1ed" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362844 1081 "4" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362844 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362844 1084 #uuid "6edc32ff-1826-5302-8b38-a4e5f595c725" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362845 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362846 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362845 1069 "q-122099" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362845 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362845 1071 "The acceleration $a$ at time $t$ of a particle $P$ moving in the $xy$-plane is given by\n\n$$\na(t)=⟨3,\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t-2}}⟩,\\,t>2.\n$$\n\nGiven that the particle has velocity $v=⟨15,1⟩$ when $t=11,$ calculate the times at which the particle is stationary." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362845 1072 #uuid "76fd517a-05e5-5caa-be51-ae532ba4527b" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362845 1074 "The particle is stationary when its velocity is zero. So first, we need to compute the velocity of the particle.\n\nTo compute the velocity vector, we need to integrate the acceleration vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int ⟨3,\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t-2}}⟩\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨\\int 3\\,\\text{d}t,\\int \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t-2}}\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3t+{C}_{1},\\sqrt{t-2}+{C}_{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve for the constants of integration using the fact that $v(11)=⟨15,1⟩.$ Substituting $t=11,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(11) & =⟨3(11)+{C}_{1},\\sqrt{11-2}+{C}_{2}⟩ \\\\ ⟨15,1⟩ & =⟨33+{C}_{1},3+{C}_{2}⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso we must have ${C}_{1}=-18$ and ${C}_{2}=-2.$ Therefore, the velocity is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =⟨3t-18,\\sqrt{t-2}-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the times at which the particle is stationary, we solve for the times at which the velocity is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =0 \\\\ ⟨3t-18,\\sqrt{t-2}-2⟩ & =⟨0,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we need\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3t-18=3(t-6) & =0\\,⇒\\,t=6, \\\\ \\sqrt{t-2}-2 & =0\\,⇒\\,t=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe only solution that satisfies both equations is $t=6,$ so this is the only value of $t$ when the particle is stationary." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362846 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362847 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362846 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362848 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362846 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362849 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362846 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362850 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362846 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362851 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362846 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362846 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362846 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362847 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362846 1080 #uuid "bf9d4ba5-fd55-5850-904b-986ef258a618" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362847 1081 "t=6" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362847 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362847 1084 #uuid "bc6f8c3f-8a6b-59cf-bc0b-fd0db0d474a9" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362848 1081 "t=10" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362848 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362848 1084 #uuid "424214f9-9d50-5467-95e0-cf55272efa8a" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362849 1081 "t=4" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362849 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362849 1084 #uuid "4aae2e57-321d-5434-85a8-2486b5ffa4bc" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362850 1081 "t=8" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362850 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362850 1084 #uuid "e1dba1cc-5a3a-58e2-8afb-f17a55ff188a" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362851 1081 "No stationary points" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362851 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362851 1084 #uuid "3056aeb4-4139-510a-a7c5-74326f7efd1b" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362852 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362853 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362852 1069 "q-122317" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362852 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362852 1071 "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis. When the displacement of $P$ from the origin $O$ is $x$ meters, its velocity is $v\\,m/s$ and its acceleration is $\\sqrt[3]{3{x}^{2}+2}\\,{m/s}^{2}.$ Which differential equation describes this motion?" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362852 1072 #uuid "176edb15-1bd9-590d-8107-8cb1c8611e83" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362852 1074 "![](images/30/30e0e58a17f1683f1c6ca58ea8e4d3df97d7edb76676b0ed6d1a75f62d0c0803.png)\n\nSince the acceleration of the particle $P$ is $\\sqrt[3]{3{x}^{2}+2}\\,{m/s}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=\\sqrt[3]{3{x}^{2}+2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule for differentiation, we can rewrite this equation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=\\sqrt[3]{3{x}^{2}+2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $v=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},$ we have\n\n$$\nv\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\sqrt[3]{3{x}^{2}+2}.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nFinally, using the fact that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({v}^{2})=2v\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2})=v\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x},\n$$\n\nwe can write our differential equation $(∗)$ as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2})=\\sqrt[3]{3{x}^{2}+2}.\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362853 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362854 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362853 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362855 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362853 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362856 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362853 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362857 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362853 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362858 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362853 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 1319413