194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362859 1071 "If $X={1,3,5,7}$ and $Y={1,2,3,4},$ then $X-Y=$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362859 1072 #uuid "1862ce9c-aa0a-58dc-aaa2-bcaac3082d73" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362859 1074 "The set $X-Y$ is the set of all elements belonging to $X$ but *not* $Y.$ Note that the elements $1,3\\in Y$ are also in $X,$ so we must remove them. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X-Y & ={1,3,5,7}-{1,2,3,4} \\\\  & ={5,7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362860 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362861 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362860 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362862 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362860 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362863 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362860 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362864 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362860 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362865 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362860 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362860 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362860 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362865 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362860 1080 #uuid "3e4a09d4-ab3e-5a14-826d-18939906ec9e" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362861 1081 "{2,4}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362861 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362861 1084 #uuid "273b54b1-0251-535f-9fcc-91d1d8241cba" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362862 1081 "{1,3,5,7}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362862 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362862 1084 #uuid "8ca1b182-bbd9-5a09-9ebc-dfe97ee018c1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362863 1081 "{1,3}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362863 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362863 1084 #uuid "1b4cc023-9622-5292-a3ba-f0b455337a45" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362864 1081 "{1,2}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362864 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362864 1084 #uuid "71329164-e8aa-5c3b-8798-48a45bf05615" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362865 1081 "{5,7}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362865 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362865 1084 #uuid "c9336807-fe1a-5dad-a1f6-a4d3123cf25f" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362866 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362867 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362866 1069 "q-126776" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362866 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362866 1071 "A random variable $X$ has the probability distribution given below.\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}0.25, & x=10 \\\\ 0.4, & x=20 \\\\ 0.35, & x=30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362866 1072 #uuid "78205dd5-88d0-5e76-92fb-fd33346bf169" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362866 1074 "If $X$ is a discrete random variable with probability mass function $f(x)$ and sample space $S,$ the expected value of ${X}^{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each squared value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x) \\\\  & ={10}^{2}\\cdot 0.25+{20}^{2}\\cdot 0.4+{30}^{2}\\cdot 0.35 \\\\  & =100\\cdot 0.25+400\\cdot 0.4+900\\cdot 0.35 \\\\  & =500.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362867 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362868 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362867 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362869 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362867 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362870 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362867 1075 #edb/ref 1759