2186045585 true] [17592186362922 1071 "Calculate ${lim}_{t\\to \\pi }f(t),$ if $f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\pi }{t} \\\\ \\frac{2t}{\\pi } \\\\ \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi -t)}{\\pi -t}\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362922 1072 #uuid "8f99695e-0a0c-536e-9ef1-383d03266523" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362922 1074 "First, recall that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{t\\to \\pi }f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to \\pi }\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\pi }{t} \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to \\pi }\\frac{2t}{\\pi } \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to \\pi }\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi -t)}{\\pi -t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we find the limits one-by-one.\n\n- For the first component, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to \\pi }\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\pi }{t} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi -\\pi }{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{0-\\pi }{\\pi } \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the second component, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to \\pi }\\frac{2t}{\\pi } & =\\frac{2\\pi }{\\pi }=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third component can be found using L'Hopital's Rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to \\pi }\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi -t)}{\\pi -t} & ={lim}_{t\\to \\pi }\\frac{{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi -t))}^{′}}{(\\pi -t)^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{t\\to \\pi }\\frac{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi -t)}{(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi -\\pi )}{1} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡0 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, ${lim}_{t\\to \\pi }f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362923 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362924 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362923 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362925 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362923 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362926 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362923 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362927 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362923 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362928 13194139533445 1759