186363020 1074 "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following  linearity properties for divergence:\n\n- $∇\\cdot (kF)=k∇\\cdot F$\n\n- $∇\\cdot (F+G)=∇\\cdot F+∇\\cdot G.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (2F)=2∇\\cdot F.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\cdot F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x{e}^{y})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-({e}^{y}+yz))+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({z}^{2}+{x}^{3}) \\\\  & =2{e}^{y}-{e}^{y}-z+2z \\\\  & ={e}^{y}+z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (2F) & =2∇\\cdot F \\\\  & =2\\cdot ({e}^{y}+z) \\\\  & =2{e}^{y}+2z.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363021 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363022 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363021 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363023 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363021 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363024 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363021 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363025 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363021 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363026 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363021 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363021 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363021 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363025 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363021 1080 #uuid "c89c2538-3d9b-5ad5-879c-1263842bba79" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363022 1081 "2z" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363022 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363022 1084 #uuid "0acefe23-9b28-502c-ba97-f67524ee9985" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363023 1081 "2{e}^{y}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363023 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363023 1084 #uuid "00e319eb-2b36-50df-a8f0-a060d2acf8e9" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [1759218636