92186363076 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363076 1071 "Using the cross product curvature formula, find the curvature of $r(t)=⟨{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩$ as a function of $t.$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363076 1072 #uuid "637c470e-0d8c-59d9-a6f9-8a2dca1476a3" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363076 1074 "The curvature $κ$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\  & ={e}^{-t}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & ={e}^{-t}\\sqrt{{(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}+{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}} \\\\  & ={e}^{-t}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡t+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & ={e}^{-t}\\sqrt{2({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the second derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-2{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\  & =2{e}^{-t}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the cross product by considering ${r}^{′}(t)$ and ${r}^{″}(t)$ as $3$-dimensional vectors with zero $z$-components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t) & =({e}^{-t}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,0⟩)\\times (2{e}^{-t}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,0⟩) \\\\  & =2{e}^{-2t}\\,\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & \\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & 0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t & -\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =2{e}^{-2t}\\,\\left|\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & \\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t & -\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k \\\\  & =2{e}^{-2t}({cos}^{2}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)k \\\\  & =2{e}^{-2t}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the magnitude of the cross product is\n\n$$\n‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖=2{e}^{-2t}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{e}^{-2t}}{{(\\sqrt{2}{e}^{-t})}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{e}^{-2t}}{2\\sqrt{2}{e}^{-3t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}{e}^{t}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363077 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363078 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363077 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363079 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363077 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363080 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363077 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363081 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363077 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363082 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363077 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363077 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363077 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363078 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363077 1080 #uuid "286f4b92-5146-53e6-94b4-5d0de177995b" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363078 1081 "\\frac{\\sqrt{