{F}_{1}+{F}_{2} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3t-7}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,5t⟩+⟨\\frac{7t-3}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,5t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{10t-10}{(t+1)(t-1)},\\,10t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{10(t-1)}{(t+1)(t-1)},\\,10t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{10}{t+1},\\,10t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy Newton's second law, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{F}{m} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot ⟨\\frac{10}{t+1},\\,10t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2}{t+1},\\,2t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo compute the velocity vector $v,$ we need to integrate the acceleration vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\int a\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int ⟨\\frac{2}{t+1},\\,2t⟩\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨\\int \\frac{2}{t+1}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int 2t\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1),\\,{t}^{2}⟩+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a (vector) constant of integration. \n\nWe can solve for $C$ by substituting $v=⟨0,\\,-1⟩\\,\\text{m/s}$ and $t=0\\,\\text{s}$ into the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨0,\\,-1⟩ & =⟨2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0+1),\\,{0}^{2}⟩+C \\\\ ⟨0,\\,-1⟩ & =⟨0,\\,0⟩+C \\\\ C & =⟨0,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity of $P$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =⟨2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1),\\,{t}^{2}⟩+⟨0,\\,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1),\\,{t}^{2}-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen $t=1,$ the velocity equals\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(1) & =⟨2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+1),\\,{1}^{2}-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the speed of $P$ when $t=1$ equals the magnitude of $v(1).$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|v(1)| & =\\sqrt{(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\,\\text{m/s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363153 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363154 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363153 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363155 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363153 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363156 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363153 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363157 13194139533445 17592186045585 tr