 coordinates of a point, then its Cartesian coordinates $(x,y,z)$ can be found by using the formulas\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,z=z.\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the projection of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](images/9c/9c4ea0ba92e19a201e3944defa6deb0bc1ee76971adaa809521722b6ac31241f.png)\n\nThe region $R$ is a right vertical cylinder of radius $3$ whose axis passes through the point $(0,0)$ in the $xy$-plane, and is\n\n- bounded below by $z=0,$ and\n\n- bounded above by $z=\\sqrt{9-({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})}=\\sqrt{9-{r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )}=\\sqrt{9-{r}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )}.$\n\nAs a result, in cylindrical polar coordinates, our region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta ,z)\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 3,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,\\,0\\le z\\le \\sqrt{9-{r}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}\\frac{z}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}V & ={∭}_{Δ}\\frac{z}{\\sqrt{{r}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{r}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }}\\,r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{9-{r}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )}}z\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{3}{[\\frac{1}{2}{z}^{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=\\sqrt{9-{r}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )}}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{2}{(\\sqrt{9-{r}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )})}^{2}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{2}(9-{r}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{[\\frac{9}{2}r-\\frac{1}{6}{r}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )]}_{r=0}^{r=3}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{9}{2}(3)-\\frac{1}{6}(3)^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{27}{2}-\\frac{9}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={[\\frac{27}{2}\\theta -\\frac{9}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )]}_{\\theta =0}^{\\theta =2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{2}(2\\pi -0)-\\frac{9}{4}(0-0) \\\\  & =27\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363356 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363357 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363356 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363358 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363356 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363359 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363356 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363360 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363356 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363361 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363356 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363356 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363356 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363360 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363356 1080 #uuid "b0c7111c-c30f-53e3-ad02-5b0477136519" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363357 1081 "9\\pi " 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363357 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363357 1084 #uuid "276b1353-c5cc-563b-8a69-6738850d94db" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363358 1081 "54\\pi " 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363358 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363358 1084 #uuid "126208a2-9813-526b-b827-e8311e0cb6c5" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363359 1081 "\\frac{19\\pi }{3}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363359 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363359 1084 #uuid "209dc6df-d901-5583-abd3-2fad14e0dcc3" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363360 1081 "27\\pi " 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363360 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363360 1084 #uu