3498 1084 #uuid "566980c0-9d00-5a29-b05a-cac367edfbb2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363499 1081 "-1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363499 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363499 1084 #uuid "dc697d16-cd1d-50e1-81a4-0a7ea90187b9" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363500 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363501 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363500 1069 "q-163181" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363500 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363500 1071 "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}.$\nThe mass density at each point is proportional to the sum of its distance from the \n$x$-axis and its distance from the $y$-axis. Find the moment of inertia of the lamina about the $x$-axis." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363500 1072 #uuid "277b81af-ece5-57d8-a083-94f5105fa453" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363500 1074 "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nFrom the description, the mass density function can be written as\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=k(|x|+|y|)=k(x+y),\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ is a constant of proportionality. We can find an expression for $k$ in terms of $M$ by integrating the density function over the plate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}k(x+y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}x+y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+xy]}_{x=0}^{x=2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{2}2+2y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =k{[2y+{y}^{2}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =k(4+4) \\\\  & =8k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k=\\frac{M}{8}$ and hence,\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=k(x+y)=\\frac{M}{8}(x+y).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{8}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{2}\\cdot (x+y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{8}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}x{y}^{2}+{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{8}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+x{y}^{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{8}{\\int }_{0}^{2}2{y}^{2}+2{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{8}{[\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{4}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{8}(\\frac{16}{3}+8) \\\\  & =\\frac{5M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363501 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363502 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363501 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363503 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363501 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363504 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363501 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363505 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363501 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363506 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363501 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363501 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363501 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363502 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363501 1080 #uuid "836bf381-5e9c-5e6d-b2b3-b979431c05d9" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363502 1081 "\\frac{5M}{3}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363502 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363502 1084 #uuid "5e0e4dc6-cc83-5e7f-b79b-720783cf7352" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363503