ut the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2x},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/3c/3cd38c4eca16f60ac918a6867e858ae3c1d4589a3a02d04f7b34f5cf7e24ac62.png)\n\nFrom the description, the mass density function can be written as \n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=k|x|=kx,\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ is a constant of proportionality. We can find an expression for $k$ in terms of $M$ by integrating the density function over the plate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2x}kx\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{2x}x\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{2}[xy]_{y=0}^{y=2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{2}x(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{2}2{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{[\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{16k}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k=\\frac{3M}{16}$ and hence,\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=kx=\\frac{3M}{16}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{16}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})(x)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{16}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{2x}{x}^{3}+x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{16}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{[{x}^{3}y+\\frac{1}{3}x{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{16}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{3}(2x)+\\frac{1}{3}x(2x)^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{16}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{14}{3}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{7M}{8}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{7M}{8}{[\\frac{1}{5}{x}^{5}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7M}{8}\\cdot \\frac{32}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{28M}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363508 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363509 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363508 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363510 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363508 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363511 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363508 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363512 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363508 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363513 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363508 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363508 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363508 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363511 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363508 1080 #uuid "c7a3feb3-84c3-54d4-90e6-341ec4dd20f8" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363509 1081 "\\frac{14M}{15}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363509 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363509 1084 #uuid "7d7207b7-4fda-5f9d-a776-fb1f6b0bb92c" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363510 1081 "\\frac{7M}{12}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363510 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363510 1084 #uuid "1e842a0a-61ed-5c50-bb33-fa3671a32175" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363511 1081 "\\frac{28M}{5}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363511 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363511 1084 #uuid "9efac7e2-97f9-57f2-8dea-ec632a1aa019" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363512 1081 "\\frac{M}{18}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363512 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363512 1084 #uuid "c8bfe486-709a-5ba4-9d2d-497eabbffd3a" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363513 1081 "\\frac{25M}{16}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363513 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363513 1084 #uuid "2750671c-4e31-5c69-bc02-fa6f4189ee66" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363514 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363515 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363514 1069 "q-163215" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363514 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363514 1071 "![](images/f2/f2882faa5326248c0a8376a8b05ce5e8008ed2c545b4ea212611334723a57185.png)\n\nA triangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region $D$ enclosed between the lines $y=0,y=2x,$ and $x=2,$ as shown above. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the origin." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363514 1072 #uuid "a7f0c8ba-8052-5102-b6bb-8f55d8855ad2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363514 1074 "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2x},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/76/760f05986cf2d58561ddcdc80b41b7f2a91ea8cc1fd5482ab115e3950d213b81.png)\n\nThe area of the triangular plate $D$ is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot 4=4.\n$$\n\nSince the plate has uniform density, every unit of area contains the same amount of mass. Therefore, the mass density is constant and is given by the total mass divided by the total area:\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{2x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{[{x}^{2}y+\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=2x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}2{x}^{3}+\\frac{8}{3}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{14}{3}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{[\\frac{7}{6}{x}^{4}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7M}{24}(16-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{14M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363515 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363516 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363515 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363517 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363515 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363518 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363515 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363519 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363515 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363520 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363515 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363515 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363515 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363519 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363515 1080 #uuid "65b269d1-bfcb-5c77-a4a9-ff25c88ac590" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363516 1081 "6M" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363516 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363516 1084 #uuid "08398c3d-3e03-5d83-8397-2ca807e951ba" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363517 1081 "\\frac{7M}{2}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363517 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363517 1084 #uuid "e8bb5c5e-4771-5a0d-8b21-0e4447b56a1b" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363518 1081 "\\frac{4M}{3}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363518 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363518 1084 #uuid "0a55a3fe-9a71-5c66-b7d5-042ecf4ed23a" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363519 1081 "\\frac{14M}{3}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363519 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363519 1084 #uuid "c032f735-7507-5c6b-a3f6-5a28802ae331" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363520 1081 "3M" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363520 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363520 1084 #uuid "291ed787-40cd-51ad-a736-6c41c7b22191" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363521 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363522 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363521 1069 "q-163216" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363521 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363521 1071 "![](images/aa/aabab0fe2815ff66ba2766ccec06046f1022440adca24921d0cd914a6009d8f1.png)\n\nA triangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region $D$ enclosed between the $y$-axis and the lines $y=x$ and $y=3,$ as shown above. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the origin." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363521 1072 #uuid "64994d24-2513-5ad7-9b86-178f34d56c41" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363521 1074 "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\,x\\le y\\le 3},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/5c/5c8b8b20bdafd15c5784ad2c83cafe52ab2afe45956dd4c7a640260840098a8f.png)\n\nThe area of the triangular plate $D$ is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3\\cdot 3=\\frac{9}{2}.\n$$\n\nSince the plate has uniform density, every unit of area contains the same amount of mass. Therefore, the mass density is constant and is given by the total mass divided by the total area:\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{2M}{9}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{x}^{3}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{x}^{3}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{[{x}^{2}y+\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{y=x}^{y=3}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(3{x}^{2}+9)-({x}^{3}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}3{x}^{2}+9-\\frac{4}{3}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{9}{[{x}^{3}+9x-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{3}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{9}(27+27-27) \\\\  & =6M.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363522 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363523 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363522 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363524 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363522 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363525 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363522 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363526 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363522 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363527 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363522 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363522 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363522 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363523 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363522 1080 #uuid "d9ba8632-e891-5861-9af1-c23727559e00" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363523 1081 "6M" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363523 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363523 1084 #uuid "4ca679f4-4be6-573e-a3d6-fcc2cce72489" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363524 1081 "\\frac{3M}{4}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363524 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363524 1084 #uuid "d7826cb4-4ec6-55a6-9edd-e0bd7b3bae4c" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363525 1081 "\\frac{2M}{3}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363525 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363525 1084 #uuid "ac4f7806-35b4-57a2-b045-f18803bfc58e" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363526 1081 "3M" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363526 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363526 1084 #uuid "91cb86fc-eede-51e3-a326-ce683480db90" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363527 1081 "2M" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363527 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363527 1084 #uuid "085e30ad-b41f-545e-9730-6b9afda8dcf8" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363528 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363529 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363528 1069 "q-163245" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363528 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363528 1071 "![](images/5b/5b8ddb36e814517af21d790374e1fb192141bd6ef0fd99e83a147c6ed5a62aea.png)\n\nConsider a plate of mass $M$ that occupies the region $D$ in the first quadrant bounded by the polar circles $r=1,$ $r=2,$ and the coordinate axes, as shown above. The mass density at any point is proportional to its distance from the $x$-axis. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the $y$-axis." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363528 1072 #uuid "f466ecc5-4b24-5385-9cf8-ddb7d1c5a54a" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363528 1074 "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (r,\\theta ),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis, in polar coordinates, is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis, in polar coordinates, is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin, in polar coordinates, is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta ={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that the region $D,$ in polar coordinates, can be expressed as\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,1\\le r\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}}.\n$$\n\nFrom the description, the mass density function can be written as $\\lambda (r,\\theta )=kr\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ where $k$ is a constant of proportionality. We can find an expression for $k$ in terms of $M$ by integrating the density function over the plate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}kr\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{r}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =k({\\int }_{1}^{2}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =k\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{r}^{3}\\,{|}_{1}^{2}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =k\\cdot \\frac{7}{3}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{7k}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\lambda (r,\\theta )=kr\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{3M}{7}r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{7}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot {r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{7}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{r}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{7}({\\int }_{1}^{2}{r}^{4}\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{7}\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}{r}^{5}\\,{|}_{1}^{2}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{3}{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta ){|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{7}\\cdot \\frac{31}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{31M}{35}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363529 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363530 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363529 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363531 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363529 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363532 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363529 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363533 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363529 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363534 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363529 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363529 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363529 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363534 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363529 1080 #uuid "ad9d5dc1-1ccb-5ea8-ad8f-aca7f98cbdb4" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363530 1081 "\\frac{32M}{27}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363530 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363530 1084 #uuid "83ea8ac1-1f81-5abd-95e4-bcb75ab9d515" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363531 1081 "\\frac{27M}{20}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363531 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363531 1084 #uuid "4e77d543-36a4-5246-9399-2c3fa0a1f926" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363532 1081 "\\frac{16M}{21}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363532 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363532 1084 #uuid "6c2750d6-a7aa-5abd-9b12-5953eae16410" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363533 1081 "\\frac{41M}{16}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363533 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363533 1084 #uuid "78940305-7e88-5a7e-841e-9a976bbfcddf" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363534 1081 "\\frac{31M}{35}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363534 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363534 1084 #uuid "25ac6f86-fd05-569c-8225-50d1be01ec9c" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363535 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363536 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363535 1069 "q-163775" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363535 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363535 1071 "The quadratic Taylor approximation of the function $f(x)$ about $x=a\\in {R}^{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈1+\\frac{1}{2}(x-a)^{T}[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -6\\end{aligned}](x-a).\n$$\n\nGiven that the eigenvalues of ${f}^{″}(a)$ are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-3$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-9,$ what type of point is $a?$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363535 1072 #uuid "1f0502ee-0a83-5915-919b-cb8a0333bfec" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363535 1074 "The point $a\\in {R}^{n}$ is a critical point of the function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ if ${f}^{′}(a)={0}^{T}.$ In such cases, we can classify $a$ as follows:\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is positive definite, then $a$ is a local minimum\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is negative definite, then $a$ is a local maximum\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is neither positive-definite nor negative-definite, then $a$ is a saddle point\n\nThe quadratic Taylor expansion of a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ about $x=a\\in {R}^{n}$ given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a)+\\frac{1}{2}(x-a)^{T}{f}^{″}(a)(x-a).\n$$\n\nSince the quadratic Taylor expansion of $f$ has no $(x-a)$ term, we can conclude that ${f}^{′}(a)={0}^{T}.$ Hence, $a$ is a critical point of $f.$\n\nFinally, notice that both the eigenvalues of ${f}^{″}(a)$ are negative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1} & =-3<0 \\\\ {\\lambda }_{2} & =-9<0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the matrix is negative definite. Therefore, $a$ is a local maximum of $f.$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363536 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363537 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363536 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363538 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363536 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363539 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363536 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363540 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363536 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363541 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363536 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363536 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363536 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363537 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363536 1080 #uuid "be669623-0526-55a8-9e58-06217378cfec" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363537 1081 "local maximum" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363537 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363537 1084 #uuid "99f22169-b8a2-5fb3-aca1-3e5599415ad8" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363538 1081 "inconclusive" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363538 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363538 1084 #uuid "abbaa7f2-5259-5b5a-bebd-07f255b181e9" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363539 1081 "not a critical point" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363539 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363539 1084 #uuid "f674340e-9bc4-5748-9997-f0404db95ca2" 13194139533445 1759