e quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ (as well as the matrix $A$) is \n\n- positive-definite if and only if ${Δ}_{i}>0$ for all $i=1,2,…,n,$\n\n- negative-definite if and only if, for all $i=1,2,…,n,$ we have ${Δ}_{i}<0$ when $i$ is odd, and ${Δ}_{i}>0$ when $i$ is even.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, ${a}_{11}=-2$ and\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|=-7.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Δ}_{1} & ={a}_{11}=-2<0, \\\\ {Δ}_{2} & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|=-7<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by Sylvester's criterion, the matrix $A$ is neither positive-definite nor negative-definite.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since the matrix $A$ is neither positive-definite nor negative-definite, the critical point $a$ is a saddle point of $f.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363543 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363544 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363543 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363545 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363543 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363546 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363543 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363547 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363543 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363548 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363543 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363543 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363543 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363545 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363543 1080 #uuid "98cace57-36bb-5a76-b3a7-cc33bc716166" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363544 1081 "None of the statements are true" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363544 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363544 1084 #uuid "2bdcb378-9b17-5091-8e17-1a127ff923c3" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [1759218636354