ef 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363588 1084 #uuid "28a698cf-cd11-5929-8167-bd140fb45ce8" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363589 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363590 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363589 1069 "q-174983" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363589 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363589 1071 "Let $I=[0,1]⊂R$ and ${X}_{i}={i}\\times [0,{i}^{2}].$ Which of the following represents ${⋂}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}?$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363589 1072 #uuid "0c924021-a1d6-52ca-a73f-6c38cfe19d10" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363589 1074 "Recall that the intersection of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *all* the sets:\n\n$$\n{⋂}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}={x\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{k}\\,\\,\\text{for all}\\,\\,k\\in I}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=1,$ we have\n\n$$\n{X}_{1}={1}\\times [0,{1}^{2}]={(1,k)\\,:\\,k\\in [0,1]}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a vertical line segment from the point $(1,0)$ to the point $(1,1)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](images/6b/6b6a47e464623fe9c572a52f7c71377136e68f41dcfd641920634b415568d7f5.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}={i}\\times [0,{i}^{2}]={(i,{k}^{2})\\,:\\,k\\in [0,i]}\n$$\n\nis the vertical line segment from the point $(i,0)$ to the point $(i,{i}^{2}).$ \n\n![](images/c6/c67cd0b545f0fc779d2977e38fab8164eb3b0161a18e32a615c71d88d1c30b68.png)\n\nThere are no points that lie in all sets. Therefore, the intersection of the indexed sets is $∅,$ the empty set." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363590 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363591 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363590 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363592 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363590 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363593 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363590 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363594 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363590 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363595 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363590 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363590 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363590 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363592 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363590 1080 #uuid "2937fc19-9446-547b-b6b5-44f5115d1bb3" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363591 1081 "images/18/186edc45b6723d68a48d4290c04bdbf9fb381f622d7684037344285c7deb66ad.png" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363591 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363591 1084 #uuid "a3333ac3-c25a-538d-ad9b-0631ad7450ff" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363592 1081 "$∅,$ the empty set" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363592 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363592 1084 #uuid "faff2f1e-83c7-51b6-b58d-6aec701467a1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363593 1081 "images/6e/6e5cb597381e0aa28cbaa19c2c8ef124be04c786543bb8488a7476f5eee32c30.png" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363593 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363593 1084 #uuid "97be09fa-bece-5e66-87e6-9fa6315b13c4" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363594 1081 "images/0b/0b689347086db4bf406a17c633b83dbc924d4c4963a64a2ca0efa7321bd6e1b3.png" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363594 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363594 1084 #uuid "8b7d5dc2-2a99-567f-a521-6bba901ee80c" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363595 1081 "images/f6/f63649f72c17dfc510df937118beb2c5cdc2338c9d4a7e03c2a2d495dccdbc64.png" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363595 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363595 1084 #uuid "e9b7157f-08b5-598c-9e76-8f4a8bba51d9" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363596 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363597 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363596 1069 "q-20515" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363596 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363596 1071 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+2y+z=-4 \\\\  & 2x+5y+3z=-10 \\\\  & 3x+6y+4z=-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363596 1072 #uuid "8557cbac-c9fb-5ae6-8b4f-ab9d7e2cdf03" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363596 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 3 & -10 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 4 & -12\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 3 & -10 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 4 & -12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 4 & -12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363597 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363598 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363597 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363599 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363597 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363600 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363597 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363601 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363597 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363602 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363597 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363597 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363597 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363599 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363597 1080 #uuid "5ee53708-7bbe-5275-be3b-4ffaa95c115d" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363598 1081 "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363598 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363598 1084 #uuid "c1c26475-90bd-5e7a-84b3-47ac0bd01588" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363599 1081 "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363599 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363599 1084 #uuid "97a92173-cc7b-5847-916b-da911b96d3d4" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363600 1081 "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363600 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363600 1084 #uuid "3f69175b-4c5a-5019-855c-5dd66c050c76" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363601 1081 "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363601 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363601 1084 #uuid "135066fa-e5ab-531e-823d-7b8a43cfbd6d" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363602 1081 "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363602 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363602 1084 #uuid "f54d27f3-bd4c-5652-a2f5-cdb2aeecffce" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363603 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363604 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363603 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363606 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363603 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363608 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363603 1069 "q-275760" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363603 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363603 1071 "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3y+2x=3 \\\\ x-2y=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | $2$ | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $1$ | {{field-3}} |  | |  |  |  | |  | $3$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $1$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $2$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |\n|  | $1$ | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |\n|  | $3$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $1$ |  |  |  |  |" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363603 1072 #uuid "4290f953-e9cc-53d8-aaec-0e2030ce4110" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363603 1074 "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+3y=3 \\\\ x-2y=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot (-2)-1\\cdot 3}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-7)}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363604 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363605 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363604 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363604 1077 "field-2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363