gin{aligned}t+8 \\\\ \\frac{4}{{t}^{2}+3} \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363639 1072 #uuid "90d60ae5-6d73-512a-9d98-e0755871b8f9" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363639 1074 "First, we find the limit of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 1}f(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 1}({t}^{2}-1) \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 1}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-1)}{t-1}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{1}^{2}-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 1}g(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 1}(t+8) \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 1}\\frac{4}{{t}^{2}+3} \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 1}11\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1+8 \\\\ \\frac{4}{{1}^{2}+3} \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we used the change of variable $u=t-1$ and the property ${lim}_{u\\to 0}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡u}{u}=1.$\n\nNow, we use properties of limits to calculate the final result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 1}[f(t)\\times g(t)] & ={lim}_{t\\to 1}f(t)\\times {lim}_{t\\to 1}g(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & \\operatorname{sin}⁡1 & 1 \\\\ 9 & 1 & 11\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 11\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 9 & 11\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}0 & \\operatorname{sin}⁡1 \\\\ 9 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sin}⁡1\\cdot 11-1\\cdot 1)\\,i-(0\\cdot 11-1\\cdot 9)\\,j+(0\\cdot 1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡1\\cdot 9)\\,k \\\\  & =(11\\operatorname{sin}⁡1-1)\\,i+9\\,j-9\\operatorname{sin}⁡1k \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}11\\operatorname{sin}⁡1-1 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -9\\operatorname{sin}⁡1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 1759218604