fore, $y(1)≈$\n{{field-2}}." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363693 1072 #uuid "3f5a6bd8-3fb9-5bda-bdfc-7b762a95a0c8" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363693 1073 true 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363693 1074 "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y(a)=c\n$$\n\nthe increment in $y$ using the Runge-Kutta (RK4) method with step size $Δx$ is computed as the weighted average of four sample slopes:\n\n$$\nΔy=\\frac{1}{6}({y}^{′}+2{y}_{1}^{′}+2{y}_{2}^{′}+{y}_{3}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- ${y}^{′}=f(x,y)$ is the estimated slope at the initial point $(x,y),$\n\n- ${y}_{1}^{′}=f({x}_{1},{y}_{1})$ is the estimated slope at $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(x+\\frac{1}{2}Δx,\\,y+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{′}\\cdot Δx),$\n\n- ${y}_{2}^{′}=f({x}_{2},{y}_{2})$ is the estimated slope at $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(x+\\frac{1}{2}Δx,\\,y+\\frac{1}{2}{y}_{1}^{′}\\cdot Δx),$\n\n- ${y}_{3}^{′}=f({x}_{3},{y}_{3})$ is the estimated slope at $({x}_{3},{y}_{3})=(x+Δx,\\,y+{y}_{2}^{′}\\cdot Δx).$\n\nAll four sample slopes are already computed. So, we just need to find the increment on $y.$\n\nWe compute $Δy$ using the Runge-Kutta method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{6}({y}^{′}+2{y}_{1}^{′}+2{y}_{2}^{′}+{y}_{3}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(1+2\\cdot \\frac{9}{4}+2\\cdot \\frac{51}{16}+\\frac{67}{8})\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot \\frac{81}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the completed first row is as given below.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{1}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{2}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{3}^{′}\\,$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $1$ | $\\frac{9}{4}$ | $\\frac{51}{16}$ | $\\frac{67}{8}$ | $\\frac{27}{8}$ |\n\nTo get the values of $x$ and $y$ in the *next* row, we add $Δx$ to $x$ and $Δy$ to $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx \\\\  & =0+1 \\\\  & =1 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\  & =1+\\frac{27}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{35}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding these rows to our table gives the following:\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{1}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{2}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{3}^{′}\\,$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $1$ | $\\frac{9}{4}$ | $\\frac{51}{16}$ | $\\frac{67}{8}$ | $\\frac{27}{8}$ |\n| $1$ | $\\frac{35}{8}$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1)≈\\frac{35}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363694 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363695 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363694 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363694 1077 "field-2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363694 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363695 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363694 1080 #uuid "f17c9d39-71b2-5e70-bdd9-d1dab26f3b47" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363695 1081 "35/8" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363695 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363695 1084 #uuid "7ed667e1-f3f3-51c6-9006-6a6298861358" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363696 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363697 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363696 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363696 1077 "field-1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363696 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363697 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363696 1080 #uuid "0ad5df7b-0f92-590a-98f4-cb6f5d1c2ae1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363697 1081 "27/8" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363697 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363697 1084 #uuid "86b21d7d-0f96-5f7a-9e87-ba787d5786ce" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363698 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363699 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363698 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363701 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363698 1068 #