=F(s),$\nthen\n$L{{e}^{at}f(t)}=F(s-a).$\n\nThis implies that multiplying a function $f(t)$ by ${e}^{at}$ shifts the corresponding Laplace transform horizontally along the $s$-axis.\n\n- If $a>0,$ the graph of $F(s)$ shifts to the right.\n\n- If $a<0,$ the graph of $F(s)$ shifts to the left.\n\nIn our case, to get the graph of $L{{e}^{-2t}f(t)},$ we must shift the graph of $F(s)$ by $2$ units to the left.\n\n![](images/a9/a902bac22ba86af8de8b49d5aba5bb34f35433230f303432e1f4327708f41a7d.png)" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363743 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363744 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363743 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363745 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363743 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363746 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363743 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363747 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363743 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363748 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363743 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363743 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363743 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363747 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363743 1080 #uuid "84509ec0-1233-5211-bf4c-8b7806b1f61b" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363744 1081 "images/8d/8daba7e586feeff02624e5d0fb508c9d2adedb23d5a79fe329f83a42e1f8256e.png" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363744 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363744 1084 #uuid "ebfe2578-7c5f-5df7-9d72-39a56be2386e" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363745 1081 "images/82/82d01729627b5871739120d2e512cf54610eaaf43f6f2f2c454b7e39803937a2.png" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363745 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363745 1084 #uuid "8e2c1dfa-8219-593c-b78b-6240e600685c" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363746 1081 "images/e6/e6d497165f1dbc9fd9db77e6a8943f6acd45262cb74ebafd4a418d6