 [17592186363924 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363932 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363924 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363935 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363924 1069 "q-338717" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363924 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363924 1071 "Consider the following boundary value problem (BVP).\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)+{e}^{-x}{y}^{′}(x)+y(x)=2,\\,-1\\le x\\le 2\n$$\n\n$$\ny(-1)-2{y}^{′}(-1)=4,\\,3y(2)+{y}^{′}(2)=0\n$$\n\nComplete the missing information below:\n\n$\\,$ The governing differential equation is {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ For this BVP, the {{field-2}} boundary conditions are {{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ The boundary value problem is {{field-4}}." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363924 1072 #uuid "d1efac48-8b43-5918-93ee-ae6f28656463" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363924 1074 "For a second-order boundary value problem, \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)+P(x){y}^{′}(x)+Q(x)y(x)=f(x),\\,a\\le x\\le b\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x),Q(x)$ and $f(x)$ are all continuous on $[a,b],$ we have the following boundary condition classifications. \n\n- Dirichlet:\n\n$$\ny(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,y(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\n- Neumann:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,{y}^{′}(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\n- Robin (mixed):\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}y(a)+{\\beta }_{1}{y}^{′}(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,{\\alpha }_{2}y(b)+{\\beta }_{2}{y}^{′}(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\gamma }_{i},{\\alpha }_{i},$ and ${\\beta }_{i}$ are real numbers with $({\\alpha }_{i},{\\beta }_{i})\\ne (0,0).$ \n\nA set of Dirichlet, Neumann, or Robin boundary conditions is homogeneous if both right-hand sides are zero (i.e., ${\\gamma }_{1}={\\gamma }_{2}=0.)$ Otherwise, they are inhomogeneous.\n\nA boundary value problem is homogeneous if the differential equation is homogeneous $(f≡0)$ and the corresponding boundary conditions are homogeneous. Otherwise, the BVP is inhomogeneous.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- 