\,$ The fundamental solutions to this BVP are {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ For this BVP, we have $det(A)=$ {{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, this BVP {{field-4}}." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363938 1072 #uuid "b5ec1be6-c77b-5453-bdcc-db467d053df0" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363938 1074 "Suppose we have the second-order homogeneous boundary value (BVP) problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=0,\\,a\\le x\\le b\n$$\n\nwith the Robin (mixed) boundary conditions\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}y(a)+{\\beta }_{1}{y}^{′}(a)=0,\\,{\\alpha }_{2}y(b)+{\\beta }_{2}{y}^{′}(b)=0\n$$\n\nwhere $P$ and $Q$ are continuous on $[a,b],$ and ${\\alpha }_{i}$ and ${\\beta }_{i}$ are real constants such that $({\\alpha }_{i},{\\beta }_{i})\\ne (0,0).$ Furthermore, suppose the fundamental solutions to the equation are ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x).$ \n\nNow, let's define the following matrix:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\,{\\alpha }_{1}{y}_{1}(a)+{\\beta }_{1}{y}_{1}^{′}(a) & {\\alpha }_{1}{y}_{2}(a)+{\\beta }_{1}{y}_{2}^{′}(a) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{2}{y}_{1}(b)+{\\beta }_{2}{y}_{1}^{′}(b) & {\\alpha }_{2}{y}_{2}(b)+{\\beta }_{2}{y}_{2}^{′}(b)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, the BVP has a unique, trivial solution $y≡0$ if and only if $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nIn other words, if the determinant equals zero, then the BVP has *infinitely many solutions*.\n\nNotice that, in our case, we have Dirichlet boundary conditions. So, setting ${\\alpha }_{i}=1,{\\beta }_{i}=0,a=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ and $b=\\frac{3\\pi }{2},$ the matrix $A$ reduces to\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & {y}_{2}\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\ {y}_{1}\\,(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}) & {y}_{2}\\,(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the fundamental solutions, we solve the auxiliary equation\n\n$$\n{m}^{2}+4=0,\n$$\n\nwhich has roots $\\pm 2i.$ Thus, the fundamental solutions are\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\text{ and }{y}_{2}(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix $A$ is\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi ) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi ) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi ) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\pi )\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nand we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =(0)(-1)-(-1)(0) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(A)=0$ we conclude that this BVP $\\text{has infinitely many solutions.}$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363939 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363940 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363939 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363941 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363939 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363942 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363939 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363943 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363939 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363944 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363939 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363939 1077 "field-3" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363939 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363943 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363939 1080 #uuid "f13639cb-b8ef-5ca4-89c3-c53bb8e1edaa" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363940 1081 "{e}^{2}(e-1)" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363940 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363940 1084 #uuid "3d048bf9-0af4-58d2-bc5b-a2f31f553d83" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363941 1081 "1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363941 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363941 1084 #uuid "ed676ff0-a712-5cfa-82de-dc9e60da14b1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363942 1081 "e-\\frac{1}{e}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363942 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363942 1084 #uuid "e36e8186-ada1-52d6-9c67-12a5c1e89670" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363943 1081 "0" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [1759218636