frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(8\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y)) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot 2y-\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot 8{e}^{x}-\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{8}{y} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=6$ and $y=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}-48{e}^{x}-8\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =0 \\\\ -6\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}-48{e}^{x} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also want to substitute for $x,$ but we are not given this value. However, we can find it by substituting $y=1$ into the equation of the curve.\n\nAt the point where $y=1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-8{e}^{x}-8\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y) & =0 \\\\ {1}^{2}-8{e}^{x}-8\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1) & =0 \\\\ 1-8{e}^{x}-0 & =0 \\\\ -8{e}^{x} & =-1 \\\\ {e}^{x} & =\\frac{1}{8} \\\\ x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{8}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{8}),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}-48{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{8})} & =0 \\\\ -6\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =48\\cdot \\frac{1}{8} \\\\ -6\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =6 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{6}{-6} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364010 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364011 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364010 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364010 1077 "field-1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364010 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364011 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364010 1080 #uuid "fa1316eb-0cbe-5a8c-b47a-2e1de32360de" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364011 1081 "-1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364011 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364011 1084 #uuid "aee8665