 3{t}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}t,\\int {csc}^{2}⁡(t)\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2{t}^{3/2}+{C}_{1},-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(t)+{C}_{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve for the constants of integration using the fact that $v(1)=⟨4,10⟩.$ Substituting $t=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(1) & =⟨2(1)^{3/2}+{C}_{1},-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(1)+{C}_{2}⟩ \\\\ ⟨4,10⟩ & =⟨2+{C}_{1},-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(1)+{C}_{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & =2+{C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{1} & =2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10 & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(1)+{C}_{2} \\\\ {C}_{2} & =10+\\operatorname{cot}⁡(1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity vector is\n\n$$\nv(t)=⟨2t\\sqrt{t}+2,\\,-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(t)+10+\\operatorname{cot}⁡(1)⟩.\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364072 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364073 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364072 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364072 1077 "field-2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364072 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364073 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364072 1080 #uuid "d3405481-7276-5270-a26f-fbc8a45d42a4" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364073 1081 "-\\operatorname{cot}(t)+10+\\operatorname{cot}(1)" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364073 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364073 1084 #uuid "c68e5a9c-c37e-5609-b152-78d048b7a1ca" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364074 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364075 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364074 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364074 1077 "field-1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364074 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364075 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364074 1080 #uuid "9bddc04d-5070-55c3-abab-43356b3093c9" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364075 1081 "2t\\sqrt{t}+2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364075 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364075 1084 #uuid "cb8de8ed-d1f7-53be-9a81-f6a5e83425ef" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364076 1068 #edb/ref 17592186364077 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364076 1068 #edb/ref 17592186364079 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364076 1069 "q-351077" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364076 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364076 1071 "The acceleration $a$ at time $t$ of a particle $P$ moving in the $xy$-plane is given by\n\n$$\na(t)=⟨\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,{e}^{t}⟩.\n$$\n\nGiven that the particle has velocity $v=⟨5,\\,e⟩$ when $t=1,$ calculate the components of the velocity vector of $P$ at time $t=4.$ Do not round the answers.\n\n$v(4)=⟨${{field-1}},{{field-2}}$⟩$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364076 1072 #uuid "e7417284-9efa-5319-acd6-3305489512a3" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364076 1074 "To compute the velocity vector, we need to integrate the acceleration vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int ⟨\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}},{e}^{t}⟩\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨\\int \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}\\,\\text{d}t,\\int {e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\sqrt{t}+{C}_{1},\\,{e}^{t}+{C}_{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve for the constants of integration using the fact that $v(1)=⟨5,e⟩.$ Substituting $t=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(1) & =⟨\\sqrt{1}+{C}_{1},\\,{e}^{1}+{C}_{2}⟩ \\\\ ⟨5,e⟩ & =⟨1+{C}_{1},\\,e+{C}_{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we must have ${C}_{1}=4$ and ${C}_{2}=0.$ Therefore, the velocity is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =⟨\\sqrt{t}+4,\\,{e}^{t}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the velocity at time $t=4$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(4) & =⟨\\sqrt{4}+4,\\,{e}^{4}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,\\,{e}^{4}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364077 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364078 13194139533445 17592186