6dd8cf" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364081 1074 "To compute the velocity vector, we need to integrate the acceleration vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int ⟨{e}^{t},3\\sqrt{t}⟩\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨\\int {e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\int 3{t}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t}+{C}_{1},\\,2t\\sqrt{t}+{C}_{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve for the constants of integration using the fact that $v(0)=⟨1,0⟩.$ Substituting $t=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(0) & =⟨{e}^{0}+{C}_{1},\\,2(0)\\sqrt{0}+{C}_{2}⟩ \\\\ ⟨1,0⟩ & =⟨1+{C}_{1},\\,0+{C}_{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we must have ${C}_{1}=0$ and ${C}_{2}=0.$ Therefore, the velocity is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =⟨{e}^{t},\\,2t\\sqrt{t}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the velocity at time $t=4$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(4) & =⟨{e}^{4},\\,2(4)\\sqrt{4}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{4},\\,16⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364082 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364083 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364082 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364082 1077 "field-2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364082 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364083 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364082 1080 #uuid "b5e3414f-c11f-5dfb-83cb-bb9e93c5814f" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364083 1081 "16" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364083 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364083 1084 #uuid "b7909c1b-9c39-5238-a960-0435cec7d722" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364084 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364085 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364084 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364084 1077 "field-1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364084 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364085 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364084 1080 #uuid "af131edb-b12c-5c92-813c-106fe168e