lve for the times at which the velocity is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =0 \\\\ ⟨2t-2,\\,-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}+1⟩ & =⟨0,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2t-2=0 & \\,⇒\\,t=1, \\\\ -\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}+1=0 & \\,⇒\\,t=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe only solution is $t=1.$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364087 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364088 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364087 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364087 1077 "field-1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364087 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364088 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364087 1080 #uuid "466e08d8-e488-5336-9585-e56e6bde3428" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364088 1081 "1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364088 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364088 1084 #uuid "1ee88a67-463d-59f1-9bc7-cf6a75a758ff" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364089 1068 #edb/ref 17592186364090 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364089 1068 #edb/ref 17592186364092 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364089 1069 "q-351850" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364089 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364089 1071 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{25}\\frac{1}{25+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\operatorname{arctan}⁡($\n{{field-2}}$)$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364089 1072 #uuid "3aa951d0-f5d2-580d-8cda-935baa717731" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364089 1074 "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{25}\\frac{1}{25+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{25}\\frac{1}{25\\cdot (1+{x}^{2}/25)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}{\\int }_{0}^{25}\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}/25}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}{\\int }_{0}^{25}\\frac{1}{1+(x/5)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{5})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{5}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{5}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=5\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $25$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $5$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{25}\\frac{1}{25+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{25}{\\int }_{0}^{25}\\frac{1}{1+(x/5)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}{\\int }_{0}^{5}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot (5\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{0}^{5}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{1+{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u{|}_{0}^{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(5)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\,arctan\\,(5)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364090 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364091 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364090 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364090 1077 "field-1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364090 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364091 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364090 1080 #uuid "d6eaf7b2-0903-5d1f-bf6c-e8f7966021aa" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364091 1081 "\\frac{1}{5}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364091 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364091 1084 #uuid "65f4d436-59f3-5763-bcdc-b3dd57872260" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364092 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364093 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364092 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533445 1