ned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =2\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{2}(2t-2)\\sqrt{(2t-2)^{2}+(2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{2}(2t-2)\\sqrt{4(t-1)^{2}+4}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{2}2(t-1)\\cdot 2\\sqrt{(t-1)^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =8\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{2}(t-1)\\sqrt{(t-1)^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe evaluate the last integral using the substitution $u=(t-1)^{2}+1.$ Then, $\\text{d}u=2(t-1)\\,\\text{d}t⟹(t-1)\\,\\text{d}t=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u$ We also need to compute new limits, given below.\n\n| **$t$** | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =8\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{2}\\sqrt{(t-1)^{2}+1}\\cdot (t-1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =8\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{2}\\sqrt{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =4\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{2}{u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =4\\pi {[\\frac{2}{3}{u}^{3/2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\pi }{3}[{(2)}^{3/2}-{(1)}^{3/2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\pi }{3}(2\\sqrt{2}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\pi }{3}(2\\sqrt{2}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364095 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364096 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364095 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364095 1077 "field-1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364095 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364096 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364095 1080 #uuid "8c9bebcb-3381-50c9-a3ff-0c3d3490a3c1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364096 1081 "\\frac{8\\pi }{3}(2\\sqrt{2}-1)" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364096 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364096 1084 #uuid "e04cba47-3267-530f-8409-5c3d5e793e34" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364097 1068 #edb/ref 17592186364098 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364097 1069 "q-352090" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364097 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 1319413953