}⁡t\\sqrt{1}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe evaluate the last integral using the substitution $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.$ Then, $\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.$ We also update the limits of integration for $u:$\n\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2\\pi u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\pi {[\\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2\\pi (\\frac{1}{2}-0) \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364098 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364099 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364098 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364098 1077 "field-1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364098 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364099 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364098 1080 #uuid "89f9fb07-f45b-568e-92ca-e253a7cffd4e" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364099 1081 "\\pi " 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364099 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364099 1084 #uuid "f882bc84-4e5a-5c6a-b34e-361d487177e6" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364100 1068 #edb/ref 17592186364101 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364100 1068 #edb/ref 17592186364103 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364100 1069 "q-352806" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364100 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364100 1071 "The velocity $v,$ in meters per second, of a particle $P$ of mass $6\\,\\text{kg}$ is given by\n\n$$\nv=⟨2{t}^{4}-{t}^{2},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t)+t⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere $t>0$ is the time in seconds. Calculate the vector of the resultant force $F$, in newtons, acting on the