071 "Consider the vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{3}$ and the block diagonal matrix $B$ shown below, where both $2\\times 2$ blocks of $B$ represent rotation-scaling matrices:\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-3+4\\text{i} \\\\ 3+7\\text{i} \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{v}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3+2\\text{i} \\\\ 1+\\text{i} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{3}$ are the eigenvectors of a matrix $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=-1+2\\text{i}$ and ${\\lambda }_{3}=3-2\\text{i},$ respectively. \nGiven that $A=PB{P}^{-1},$ which of the following could be the matrix $P?$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364182 1072 #uuid "d9ffa63b-d02b-5e1e-8168-a893ab9c9ace" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364182 1074 "Recall that if $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ real matrix that has complex eigenvalues \n\n$\\,$ ${\\lambda }_{1}={\\overset{―}{\\lambda }}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{\\lambda }_{3}={\\overset{―}{\\lambda }}_{4}$ \n\nwith corresponding eigenvectors \n\n$\\,$ ${v}_{1}={\\overset{―}{v}}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{v}_{3}={\\overset{―}{v}}_{4},$ \n\nthen $A=PB{P}^{-1},$ where\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}\\text{Re}({\\lambda }_{1}) & \\text{Im}({\\lambda }_{1}) & 0 & 0 \\\\ -\\text{Im}({\\lambda }_{1}) & \\text{Re}({\\lambda }_{1}) & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\text{Re}({\\lambda }_{3}) & \\text{Im}({\\lambda }_{3}) \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\text{Im}({\\lambda }_{3}) & \\text{Re}({\\lambda }_{3})\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | \\\\ \\text{Re}({v}_{1}) & \\text{Im}({v}_{1}) & \\text{Re}({v}_{3}) & \\text{Im}({v}_{3}) \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSwapping the blocks on the main diagonal of $B$ will result in switching the corresponding columns in $P.$\n\nFrom our block diagonal matrix\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwe deduce that the first and second columns of $P$ correspond to the complex eigenvector ${v}_{1},$ and the third and forth columns of $P$ correspond to the complex eigenvector ${v}_{3}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364183 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364184 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364183 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364185 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364183 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364186 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364183 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364187 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364183 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364188 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364183 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364183 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364183 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364184 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364183 1080 #uuid "412f7b7b-ba07-563c-9f88-1a639c80c619" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364184 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364184 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364184 1084 #uuid "4debd8f4-2deb-5319-979a-5631a200d485" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364185 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 5\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364185 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364185 1084 #uuid "373e700f-b167-5568-9d74-8640309d6744" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364186 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 7 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364186 1083 #edb/ref 175921860