he system corresponding to the final matrix equation using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 8 & -4\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\,\\,[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\,\\,[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has two pivot columns (the $1$st and $2$nd). Thus, ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable.\n\n From the second row, we have \n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=-3.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-(-3)+2{x}_{3}=-1\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-4-2{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-4-2{x}_{3} \\\\ -3 \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+4c=(-2)+(-3)+4\\cdot 0=-5.\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364216 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364217 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364216 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364218 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364216 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364219 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364216 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364220 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364216 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364221 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364216 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364216 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364216 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364218 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364216 1080 #uuid "1812231c-b731-57f0-8e96-cc3da0e4fe33" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364217 1081 "-7" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [1759