ratorname{sin}⁡2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =⟨4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4}),\\,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{4}⟩=⟨0,\\,-\\sqrt{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the cross product by considering ${r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})$ and ${r}^{″}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})$ as $3$-dimensional vectors with zero $z$-components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\times {r}^{″}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =⟨2,\\,\\sqrt{2},0⟩\\times ⟨0,\\,-\\sqrt{2},\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & \\sqrt{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\sqrt{2} & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}2 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 0 & -\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k \\\\  & =-2\\sqrt{2}\\,k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\times {r}^{″}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})‖ & =2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\times {r}^{″}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})‖}{{‖{r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})‖}^{3}}=\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{(\\sqrt{6})^{3}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364277 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364278 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364277 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364279 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364277 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364280 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364277 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364281 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364277 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364282 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364277 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364277 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364277 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364282 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364277 1080 #uuid "b145a936-f168-513a-86fa-b22a05f774eb" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364278 1