 a saddle point of $f$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364445 1072 #uuid "7ba712ba-8939-58aa-ab47-15caf19c7eaa" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364445 1074 "The second partial derivative test states that if $a\\in {R}^{2}$ is a stationary point of $f(x,y)$ with Hessian determinant $H(a),$ we have the following:\n\n- If $H(a)>0,$ then:\n\n- if $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(a)<0,$ then $f$ has a local maximum at $a$\n\n- if $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(a)>0,$ then $f$ has a local minimum at $a$\n\n- If $H(a)<0,$ then $f$ has a saddle point at $a$\n\n- If $H(a)=0,$ then the second partial derivatives test is inconclusive.\n\nFirst, we notice that since ${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-\\frac{y}{x} & \\frac{x}{y}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\end{aligned}],$ we must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-\\frac{y}{x},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{x}{y}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-\\frac{y}{x})=\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{x}{y}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)=-\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{x}{y}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{y}-\\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}} & \\frac{1}{y}-\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}-\\frac{1}{x} & -\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the second derivative at $(e,e),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(e,e)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{e} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{e}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Computing the determinant of ${f}^{″}(e,e),$ we get\n\n$$\nH(e,e)=det({f}^{″}(e,e))=\\frac{1}{e}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{e})-{0}^{2}=-\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}<0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, we have $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(e,e)=({f}^{″}(e,e))_{11}=\\frac{1}{e}>0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since $H(e,e)<0,$ the point $(e,e)$ is a saddle point by the second partial derivative test.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364446 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364447 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364446 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364448 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364446 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364449 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364446 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364450 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364446 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364451 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364446 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364446 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364446 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364447 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364446 1080 #uuid "7ddccf08-4947-5f37-a7aa-fb071af9ea51" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364447 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364447 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364447 1084 #uuid "185166b1-330b-5a2e-aba4-89d652f19ac4" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364448 1081 "I only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364448 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364448 1084 #uuid "9630115b-06b1-567f-8a74-0acec19e9110" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364449 1081 "III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364449 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364449 1084 #uuid "d7396ab7-22ea-5487-9b31-a25ba1cc7112" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364450 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364450 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364450 1084 #uuid "43dbafbd-2089-52a8-9d77-a52d3800d5a6" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364451 1081 "II only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364451 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364451 1084 #uuid "7e8e83f2-4978-5751-aa7a-0a804d3f67c5" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364452 1068 #edb/ref 17592186364453 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364452 1069 "q-81166" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364452 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364452 1071 "The function \n$f(x,y)$\nhas the first derivative\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+2xy & 2xy+{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nand has a stationary point at $(0,0).$ If $H$ denotes the Hessian determinant of $f,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $H(0,0)>0$\n- $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(0,0)<0$\n- The second partial derivative test at point $(0,0)$ is inconclusive" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364452 1072 #uuid "8ce3eb01-5fdc-5cad-ba01-77459c09b714" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364452 1074 "The second partial derivative test states that if $a\\in {R}^{2}$ is a stationary point of $f(x,y)$ with Hessian determinant $H(a),$ we have the following:\n\n- If $H(a)>0,$ then:\n\n- if $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(a)<0,$ then $f$ has a local maximum at $a$\n\n- if $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(a)>0,$ then $f$ has a local minimum at $a$\n\n- If $H(a)<0,$ then $f$ has a saddle point at $a$\n\n- If $H(a)=0,$ then the second partial derivatives test is inconclusive.\n\nFirst, we notice that since ${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+2xy & 2xy+{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}],$ we must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+2xy,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2xy+{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+2xy)=6x+2y \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2xy+{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2})=2x+6y \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2xy+{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2})=2y+2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6x+2y & 2x+2y \\\\ 2x+2y & 2x+6y\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the second derivative at $(0,0),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(0,0)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Computing the determinant of ${f}^{″}(0,0),$ we get\n\n$$\nH(0,0)=det({f}^{″}(0,0))=0\\cdot 0-{0}^{2}=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. We have $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(1,0)=({f}^{″}(0,0))_{11}=0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $H(0,0)=0,$ the second partial derivatives test is inconclusive.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364453 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364454 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364453 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364455 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364453 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364456 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364453 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364457 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364453 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364458 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364453 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364453 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364453 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364456 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364453 1080 #uuid "d845ac00-dd1f-5c10-a6d3-8682a4f10f0a" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364454 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364454 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364454 1084 #uuid "b30adad5-8524-5ce6-a501-9cad20e54adb" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364455 1081 "I only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364455 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364455 1084 #uuid "523b7f87-e3f5-5297-aa71-e8fa8c048b6a" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364456 1081 "III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364456 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364456 1084 #uuid "3aaabbd4-a86d-5914-8c28-fe26ad0b617b" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364457 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364457 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364457 1084 #uuid "e1c46f72-6bcf-5e6a-a7a0-535cb438b330" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364458 1081 "II only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364458 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364458 1084 #uuid "e829cb02-6ee3-5216-9d49-6802eaa5ad5b" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364459 1068 #edb/ref 17592186364460 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364459 1069 "q-81787" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364459 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364459 1071 "Let $A$  be the set of all multiples of $3$ greater than $0$ and let $B$  be the set of all multiples of $6$ greater than $0.$ What is $A-B?$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364459 1072 #uuid "7ff5b607-36ee-5a12-823c-f5a13db977fa" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364459 1074 "The multiples of $3$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nA={3,6,9,12,15,18,21,24,…}.\n$$\n\nLikewise, multiples of $6$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nB={6,12,18,24,…}.\n$$\n\nNow,