5 17592186045585 true] [17592186364539 1068 #edb/ref 17592186364540 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364539 1069 "q-95020" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364539 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364539 1071 "Given that $u(r,\\theta )=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta ,$ find $\\frac{∂u}{∂y},$ where $(x,y)$ are Cartesian coordinates and $(r,\\theta )$ are the corresponding plane polar coordinates." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364539 1072 #uuid "d6f35556-89a1-5c4e-ad2e-ad3a5182772a" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364539 1074 "We will make use of the following chain rule formula:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂u}{∂y}=\\frac{∂u}{∂r}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\frac{1}{r}\\frac{∂u}{∂\\theta }\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $u$ with respect to $r$ and $\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂r}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta ,\\,\\frac{∂u}{∂\\theta }=4r\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, substituting these into our chain rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂y} & =(\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\frac{1}{r}(4r\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\theta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta +4\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364540 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364541 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364540 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364542 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364540 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364543 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364540 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364544 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364540 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364545 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364540 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364540 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186