445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364546 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364546 1071 "Given that $u(r,\\theta )=r(2+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ),$ find $\\frac{∂u}{∂x},$ where $(x,y)$ are Cartesian coordinates and $(r,\\theta )$ are the corresponding plane polar coordinates." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364546 1072 #uuid "d4815c77-06a6-5342-87f5-965d49f4d616" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364546 1074 "We will make use of the following chain rule formula:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂u}{∂x}=\\frac{∂u}{∂r}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\frac{1}{r}\\frac{∂u}{∂\\theta }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $u$ with respect to $r$ and $\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂r}=2+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\frac{∂u}{∂\\theta }=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, substituting these into our chain rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & =(2+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\frac{1}{r}(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364547 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364548 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364547 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364549 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364547 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364550 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364547 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364551 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364547 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364552 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364547 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364547 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364547 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364549 13194139533445 175921