,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & 12 \\\\ 12 & 16\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}9-\\lambda  & 12 \\\\ 12 & 16-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (9-\\lambda )(16-\\lambda )-144 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-9\\lambda -16\\lambda +144-144 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-25\\lambda  & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -25) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =25,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{25}=5 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364568 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364569 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364568 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364570 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364568 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364571 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364568 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364572 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364568 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364573 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364568 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364568 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364568 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364570 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364568 1080 #uuid "08930f82-1a1a-57e2-874c-8663b93ed935" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364569 1081 "$\\sqrt{10}$ and $1$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364569 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364569 1084 #uuid "5aacda77-04a2-5890-a544-02a590c4abbe" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364570 1081 "$5$ and $0$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364570 1083 #e